  "period_note": "Balance sheet is the period-end snapshot (reported) as at 30 September 2025, from Midland Bank's own genuinely-filed, BSEC/DSE/CSE-submitted quarterly financial statements (Un-Audited). Income-statement items are CUMULATIVE from 1 January 2025 (1 January to 30 September 2025), flagged via the _cumulative suffix. SOLO / STANDALONE basis -- 'Midland Bank PLC.' / 'Midland Bank Limited' single-entity statements, distinct from the Consolidated statements the bank has also prepared since Q1 2024 (covering its subsidiary Midland Bank Asset Management Company Ltd., BSEC-licensed 4 August 2024); this file uses only the Solo figures, matching the bank's main annual Q4 series basis. provision_charge_cumulative and tax_expense_cumulative are the report's own printed 'Total Provision' and 'Provision for Tax' lines (reported, not calculated, unlike the annual Q4 series which has to derive these because its summary table omits them). Non-Banking Asset jumps from 12.59m (Dec-2024) to 108.96m this quarter, consistent with a foreclosed-asset acquisition (not separately explained in the pages reviewed). This quarter's own filing's Dec-2024 comparative NAV per share reads 14.69 (not the 15.13 in the existing 2024_Q4.json) -- this is the same mechanical artifact as noted for 2026 above (the ratio is computed by dividing the historical Dec-2024 equity by the CURRENT, post-bonus share count rather than the share count that actually applied at Dec-2024: 9,676,780,648 / 658,859,845 = 14.69); it is not a restatement of equity or profit, and 2024_Q4.json's own contemporaneous 15.13 is left untouched.",
